= pregi_franka
Once, when Franek thought nobody was looking, Jaromir saw him scratching his forearm. Down it ran three long, fresh weals, as if from claws.
“Caught it on a nail,” he grunted when he met his friend’s eye, and pulled his sleeve down.
That evening Antek came to the fence. For a long time he stood without a word, picking the bark off a paling.
“He doesn’t sleep at night,” he said at last. “Sits out on the ledge by the wall. Till dawn. I ask him what for—the saw, he says. But the saw stands still at night.” He raised his eyes to Jaromir. “He won’t listen to me. I’m just a whelp. Maybe he’ll listen to you.” # dalej
