# tlo: sciecie_debu
~ zapiski += pan_lasu_2
On Monday half the village gathered under the Old Oak. { franek_scial_dab: Franek and another sawyer | Two sawyers from the sawmill } took their places with axes on either side of the trunk, while Mr Urbaniak stood to one side, glancing every other moment at the watch on his gold chain.
Before the sawyers could swing, Hanka slipped out of the crowd. She went up to the trunk, laid both palms on the bark and whispered something to it—briefly, with her eyes shut. Urbaniak ordered her pulled away, but no one moved until she came back among the people of her own accord.
“I told it that it wasn’t me,” she explained to Jaromir afterwards, red to the ears. “So it knows who to look for.”
The first blow glanced off the bark as off a stone. The second too. Only at the third did the blade bite into the wood—and from the wound spurted sap, thick and dark red as blood.{ franek_scial_dab: It splashed Franek full in the face. The lad stumbled back, wiped his eyes with his sleeve and gave a nervous laugh, but Jaromir saw that his hands were shaking.| It splashed over the sawyers’ boots, and one of them leapt back with an oath.} # pokaz: sok
They hewed until dusk. The oak groaned at every stroke, so that the women stopped their ears and the dogs in the village howled as at a funeral. When at last it came down, the ground shook right up to the cottages, and from the direction of the forest came a cry—drawn-out, mournful, as though the woods had lost something they would never get back. Then silence fell. Even the birds went quiet. # pokaz: upadek
Only the stump remained—broad as a table, with hundreds of rings that wound inwards into a tight spiral.{ ekwipunek ? kora: Just like the one on the pine by the path and on the post of the wayside shrine.} From among the roots spilled a handful of last year’s acorns—sound and glossy, as if someone had kept them there. “What you take from under the Oak, you owe the Oak,” whispered Hanka, who stood close beside him. “So they say. For your whole life.”
